  "title": "Wake up, sleep, wash",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "'At seven o'clock' = **সাতটায়** (*shattay*): number + **-টা** + locative **-য়**. Add the part of the day in front: **সকাল সাতটায়** 'at 7 a.m.', **রাত দশটায়** 'at 10 p.m.'\n\nTo wake up is **ঘুম থেকে ওঠা** — literally 'rise from sleep'. Watch the vowel: **আমি উঠি** but **আপনি ওঠেন**. Many common verbs swap o↔u or e↔i like this; more in Lesson 4.\n\n**কখন** (*kokhon*) 'when?' goes before the verb: **আপনি কখন ঘুমান?** 'When do you sleep?'\n\n**গোসল করা** (*gosol kora*) is the everyday Bangladeshi word for bathing / showering. Kolkata (and many Hindu speakers) say **স্নান করা** (*snan kora*).",
